The figure illustrates the active transport and distribution of Nano-11 nanoparticles in the draining lymph node over time. Flow cytometry data show that the percentage of Nano-11-containing myeloid cells peaks on day 2 post-injection, with migratory dendritic cells (MigDCs) comprising the majority (60-80%) of these Nano-11-positive cells. MigDCs also exhibit the highest mean fluorescence intensity (MFI) of Nano-11 per cell, indicating their efficient uptake of the nanoparticles compared to lymphoid tissue resident DCs and monocytes/macrophages. This active targeting of immunopotentiating MigDCs highlights a key mechanism of Nano-11's adjuvant effect.